    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27ctbJ968Ep7DYfsGqXU6xM)_\n\nFollow-up to #335 (backfill all children).\n\n## Problem\nNotes made by `sp-litnotes-meta-backfill-all-children` came out with `#+title: Notes on <author>, <title>` and a `#+print_bibliography:` line. Both come from citar's own file-note template (`sp-citar-note`, \"Notes on ...\"), not from `citar-vulpea`, which only makes a title from `citar-vulpea-note-title-template`. So the backfill was using citar's file source.\n\n`#+print_bibliography:` is the Org-cite marker that prints the bibliography of the works cited in that note. A litnote cites nothing, so it is not needed.\n\n## What changes\n- The backfill makes each note with the `citar-vulpea` notes source when it is registered, whatever `citar-notes-source` is.\n- Each new note is tidied afterwards: a `Notes on ...` title is replaced and `#+print_bibliography:` lines are removed. A title that does not start with \"Notes on\" is left alone.\n- New option `sp-litnotes-meta-new-title`: `title` (default, the BibTeX title alone, as asked) or `standard` (\"Last (Year) Title\", what `sp-litnotes-titles-convert` writes).\n- Literate doc updated; one new ERT test.\n\n## Testing\n- `sp-litnotes-meta` ERT tests pass (14/14, Emacs 29.3, stubbed citar and Vulpea); `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes.\n- Not run with the real citar-vulpea on the real vault. The cause (citar's file source being used) is inferred from the \"Notes on\" title and the citar-vulpea source code; the tidy step fixes the result either way.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAsbQDho5VHotsU68a)_",
